## SM50 cockpit and front end

The stock handlebar_std and fork_std on the garage project bike now have new geometry. The cockpit has tapered alloy bars, ribbed grips, clutch and brake levers, cable runs, switchgear and a digital dash housing. The fork assembly has separate stanchions, guards, an angular blue and white number-plate headlight and a high supermoto fender. Both assets preserve their BasePart interface, pivots, existing Bolt_* and grip markers. New Lever_Brake_Pivot and Lever_Clutch_Pivot attachments mark the lever hinges. The existing headlight action uses the preset RidingHeadlight attachment at the lens.

Studio Play verified the normal garage spawn, zero decorative colliders, 34-degree rotation following the mount welds, and 17.8 mm vertical fender clearance above the front tire at 120 mm compression. The fork and bar use welded Studio geometry and built-in materials. First-person visual QA, lever motion, rider animation, the rest of the bike and PBR maps remain open.

